prog: STRING_MIDDLE

This is an invalid way to start a statement

prog: WITH WITH

`with` expressions should be of the form: `with ($ctxVar = newVal) { ... }`

prog: WITH LPAREN WITH

Only context variables (starting with `$`) can be declared in a `with` expression

prog: WITH LPAREN CONTEXT_ID WITH

Only context variable assignments are allowed in `with` expressions

prog: WITH LPAREN CONTEXT_ID EQUALS STRING_MIDDLE

This is not a valid expression for an assignment

prog: STRING_START STRING_MIDDLE

String interpolation was started but never finished

prog: LPAREN STRING_MIDDLE

What is in between parentheses is not an expression (or you have an unclosed parenthesis in the middle of string interpolation)

prog: LET WITH

The `let` keyword must be followed by a valid identifier name

prog: LET ID WITH

Expected an `=` to complete the `let` expression

prog: LET ID EQUALS STRING_MIDDLE

[UNREACHABLE]

prog: IF STRING_MIDDLE

[UNREACHABLE]

prog: BREAK FUNC WITH

An expression was expected here; function expressions should be unnamed (e.g. `let f = func(x) {x + 1}`)

prog: STRING_START CONTEXT_ID RPAREN

String interpolation was started but never finished

prog: LCURLY CONTEXT_ID STRING_MIDDLE

This is not a valid `HashMap` literal expression--did you want to make this a `do {...}` expression?
